ry between old tail and new chunk. Hmm, boundary: the last pending fragment + start of new chunk. Simplest: search new chunk for newline; if found at position i, then complete line = concat(all pending fragments) + new_chunk[:i]. Since we join at most once per newline... but if a chunk contains many newlines, we join pending fragments once, then split the rest. Actually:\n\n```python\ndef feed(self, chunk):\n    self._pending.append(self._decoder.decode(chunk))\n    out = []\n    if \"\\n\" in joined-part...\n```\n\nHmm, let me write it concretely:\n\n```python\nclass JsonlStream:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._dec = codecs.getincrementaldecoder(\"utf-8\")()\n        self._parts = []  # decoded text chunks, no \"\\n\" in any, and no complete line among them\n\n    def feed(self, chunk):\n        text = self._dec.decode(chunk)\n        out = []\n        # find newlines in `text`\n        nl = text.find(\"\\n\")\n        if nl == -1:\n            self._parts.append(text)\n        else:\n            self._parts.append(text[:nl])\n            line = \"\".join(self._parts)\n            rest = text[nl + 1:]\n            while True:\n                i = rest.find(\"\\n\")\n                if i == -1:\n                    break\n                s = line.strip()\n                if s:\n                    out.append(json.loads(s))\n                line = rest[:i]\n                rest = rest[i + 1:]\n            self._parts = [line + rest]  # wait no\n```\n\nHmm, getting convoluted. Let me restructure: after the first newline, the remainder can be processed with split:\n\n```python\ndef feed(self, chunk):\n    text = self._dec.decode(chunk)\n    out = []\n    if \"\\n\" not in text:\n        if text:\n            self._parts.append(text)\n        return out\n    # complete line spanning all pending parts + head of text\n    self._parts.append(text)\n    joined = \"\".join(self._parts)\n    lines = joined.split(\"\\n\")\n    tail = lines.pop()  # incomplete remainder