{"type":"event","event":{"type":"message_update","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The design keeps `_parts` as a list of decoded fragments guaranteed to contain no newline, so each fragment is joined at most once — amortized O(n) overall, no quadratic buffer copying. The incremental decoder handles split codepoints.\n\nNow run the public test plus my own edge-case suite and a stress test.","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The fix buffers decoded fragments that contain no newline, so each fragment is joined at most once (amortized linear, no quadratic buffer copying). Now I'll run the public test plus my own edge-case and stress verification."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"[CALL_00162]","name":"shell_command","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/flashbench_glm53_resume_3996690/t02 && python3 test_public.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json, random, string, io, sys\nfrom stream import JsonlStream\n\ndef ref(data: bytes):\n    out = []\n    for line in data.split(b\"\\n\")[:-1]:\n        s = line.strip()\n        if s:\n            out.append(json.loads(s.decode(\"utf-8\")))\n    return out\n\n# 1. record and codepoint split across chunks\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"a\":1}') == []\nassert s.feed(b'\\n{\"b\":') == [{\"a\":1}]\nassert s.feed(b'2}\\n') == [{\"b\":2}]\n\n# 2. multi-byte utf-8 split mid-codepoint\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"s\":\"\\xe4\\xb8') == []\nassert s.feed(b'\\xad\\xe6\\x96\\x87\"}\\n') == [{\"s\":\"中文\"}]\n\n# 3. blank / whitespace-only lines ignored, CRLF tolerated\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'\\n{\"a\":1}\\r\\n   \\n\\n{\"b\":2}\\n') == [{\"a\":1},{\"b\":2}]\nassert s.feed(b'') == []\n\n# 4. nested newlines inside JSON strings must be escaped -> splitting safe\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"t\":\"a\\\\nb\"}\\n{\"u\":1}\\n') == [{\"t\":\"a\\nb\"},{\"u\":1}]\n\n# 5. randomized stress vs reference, random chunk sizes\nrandom.seed(7)\nfor trial in range(200):\n    n = random.randint(0, 30)\n    recs = []\n    for _ in range(n):\n        r = {\"id\": random.randint(0, 999),\n             \"s\": \"\".join(random.choice(\"日本語äöü{}\\\"\\n\\\\ abc\") for _ in range(random.randint(0, 20)))}\n        if random.random() < 0.1: r = {}\n        recs.append(r)\n    data = b\"\".join(json.dumps(r, ensure_ascii=False).encode(\"utf-8\") + b\"\\n\" for r in recs)\n    data += b\"\\n\\n\"  # sprinkle blank lines\n    s = JsonlStream()\n    got = []\n    i = 0\n    while i < len(data):\n        k = random.randint(1, 7)\n        got += s.feed(data[i:i+k])\n        i += k\n    assert got == ref(data), (trial, got, ref(data))\n\n# 6. no trailing newline at end of last feed -> held, not emitted\ns = JsonlStream()\nassert s.feed(b'{\"a\":1}\\n{\"b\":2}') == [{\"a\":1}]\nassert s.feed(b'\\n') == [{\"b\":2}]\n\n# 7. linear scaling check: 8MB single record in 1KB chunks\nblob = json.dumps({\"pad\": \"x\" * 8_000_000}).encode(\"utf-8\")\ns = JsonlStream()\nn_chunks = 0\nfor i in range(0, len(blob), 1024):\n    s.feed(blob[i:i+1024]); n_chunks += 1\nres = s.feed(b\"\\n\")\nassert len(res) == 1 and res[0][\"pad\"] == \"x\" * 8_000_000\n\nprint(\"ALL_EDGE_TESTS_OK\")\nEOF","description":"Run public test plus edge-case and randomized stress verification","timeout":120000}}]}}
